## 4. CI: PostgREST download checksum failures (root cause NOT proven; hardening + diagnosis)
facts: main run 42564812543 attempt 1 (f9223dfe) and PR #341 run 42578842993 attempt 1 (39fb7193, job 129044869321) both failed in job storage:
  "sha256sum: WARNING: 1 computed checksum did NOT match / /tmp/pgrst.tar.xz: FAILED". The PR-run step (curl + check) took 0.13 s
  (07:58:38.5757 -> 07:58:38.7048). The real archive is 3,772,512 bytes, so 0.13 s does NOT by itself prove a bad body (an earlier draft of this
  note said "17 MB cannot download in 0.13 s" — wrong: 17 MB is the extracted binary). Attempt 2 of each run passed all jobs; attempt 1 stays recorded as failed.
  ROOT CAUSE NOT PROVEN: the old step logs neither HTTP status nor size nor actual digest.
  (publish was skipped in both and is not counted as a pass.)
plausible mechanism, demonstrated locally: `curl -sSL -o y <missing release asset>` -> rc=0, file size 9 bytes (error page saved);
                            `curl -fsSL --retry ...` on the same URL -> rc=22 "The requested URL returned error: 404".
fix — hardening + diagnosis, not a proven root-cause fix (.github/workflows/ci.yml step "Install PostgREST v12.2.3 (checksum-pinned)"): curl -f (fail on HTTP error), --retry 5 --retry-all-errors --retry-delay 5
  --connect-timeout 20; on mismatch print size + actual sha256 + `file` and exit 1. The pinned sha256 is unchanged and still mandatory; nothing is skipped.
local check of the new step: downloaded, "/tmp/pgrst.tar.xz: OK", extracted. YAML parses.
not proven: what body was actually downloaded, and whether the upstream error was transient. The new step makes the next failure self-describing
  (HTTP error -> curl rc=22 after retries; bad bytes -> size + sha256 + file type printed).

